{
  "title": "89: al-Fajr الفجر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالْفَجْرِۙ‏(1)\nWAL FAJRE.\nBy the Daybreak\nوَلَيَالٍ عَشْرٍۙ‏(2)\nWA LAYAALIN A’SRINW.\nAnd (by) the Ten Nights\nوَّالشَّفْعِ وَالْوَتْرِۙ‏(3)\nWASH SHAF-E’ WAL WATRE.\nAnd (by) the even and the odd\nوَالَّيْلِ اِذَا يَسْرِۚ‏(4)\nWAL LAYLE EZAA YASR.\nAnd (by) the Night as it passeth away\nهَلْ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ قَسَمٌ لِّذِىْ حِجْرٍؕ‏(5)\nHAL FEE ZAALEKA QASAMUL LEZEE HIJR.\nVerily there is in this an oath for those who possess understanding\nاَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِعَادٍۙ‏(6)\nALAM TARA KAYFA FA-A’LA RABBOKA BE-A’ADIN.\nHast not thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) seen how did deal thy Lord with the (people) ‘Ad’?\nاِرَمَ ذَاتِ الْعِمَادِۙ‏(7)\nERAMA ZAATIL E’MAADIL.\n(Of) Iram with tall statures\nالَّتِىْ لَمْ يُخْلَقْ مِثْلُهَا فِى الْبِلَادِۙ‏(8)\nLATEE LAM YUKHLAQ MISLOHAA FIL BELAADE.\nThe like of which were not created in any of the (other) cities (of the world)\nوَثَمُوْدَ الَّذِيْنَ جَابُوا الصَّخْرَ بِالْوَادِۙ‏(9)\nWA SAMOODAL LAZEENA JAABUS SAKHRA BIL-WAADE.\nAnd the (Tribe) Thamood who hewed out the rocks in the valley\nوَفِرْعَوْنَ ذِى الْاَوْتَادِۙ‏(10)\nWA FIR-A’WNA ZIL AWTAADIL.\nAnd Pharaoh the owner of the stakes\nالَّذِيْنَ طَغَوْا فِى الْبِلَادِۙ‏(11)\nLAZEENA TAGHAW FIL BELAADE.\nWho (all) transgressed in the cities\nفَاَكْثَرُوْا فِيْهَا الْفَسَادَۙ‏(12)\nFA-AKSAROO FEEHAL FASAADA.\nAnd multiplied wickedness therein\nفَصَبَّ عَلَيْهِمْ رَبُّكَ سَوْطَ عَذَابٍ ۙۚ‏(13)\nFA-SABBA A’LAYHIM RABBOKA SAWTA A’ZAAB.\nSo, thy Lord let fall on them the whip of a chastisement\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَبِالْمِرْصَادِؕ‏(14)\nINNA RABBAKA LA-BIL MIRSAAD.\nVerily, thy Lord is (ever) on watch\nفَاَمَّا الْاِنْسَانُ اِذَا مَا ابْتَلٰٮهُ رَبُّهٗ فَاَكْرَمَهٗ وَنَعَّمَهٗ ۙ فَيَقُوْلُ رَبِّىْۤ اَكْرَمَنِؕ‏(15)\nFA-AMMAL INSAANO EZAA MAB TALAAHO RABBOHU FA-AKRAMAHU WA NA’-A’MAHU, FA-YAQOOLO RABBEE AKRAMAN.\nAnd as for man, when trieth him his Lord, and honoureth him, and is bounteous unto him, then saith he: ‘‘My Lord hath honoured me!\nوَاَمَّاۤ اِذَا مَا ابْتَلٰٮهُ فَقَدَرَ عَلَيْهِ رِزْقَهٗ ۙ فَيَقُوْلُ رَبِّىْۤ اَهَانَنِۚ‏(16)\nWA AMMAA EZAA MAB TALAAHO FA-QADARA A’LAYHE RIZQAHU, FA-YAQOOLO RABBEE AHAANAN.\nBut when trieth him, and then straiteneth unto him his sustenance, then saith he: ‘‘My Lord hath disgraced me!\nكَلَّا بَلْ لَّا تُكْرِمُوْنَ الْيَتِيْمَۙ‏(17)\nKALLAA BAL LAA TUKREMOONAL YATEEMA.\nNay! rather ye honour not the orphan\nوَلَا تَحٰٓضُّوْنَ عَلٰى طَعَامِ الْمِسْكِيْنِۙ‏(18)\nWA LAA TAHAAZ-ZOONA A’LAA TA-A’AMIL MISKEENE.\nNor urge ye one another to feed the poor!\nوَتَاْكُلُوْنَ التُّرَاثَ اَكْلًا لَّمًّا ۙ‏(19)\nWA TAAKOLOONAT TORAASA AKLAL LAMMANW.\nAnd ye devour heritage, devouring (everything) in greed (indiscriminately)\nوَّتُحِبُّوْنَ الْمَالَ حُبًّا جَمًّا ؕ‏(20)\nWA TOHIBBOONAL MAALA HUBBAN JAMMAA.\nAnd ye love wealth with exceeding love\nكَلَّاۤ اِذَا دُكَّتِ الْاَرْضُ دَكًّا دَكًّا ۙ‏(21)\nKALLAAA EZAA DUKKATIL ARZO DAKKAN DAKKANW.\nNay! when the earth shall be pounded to powder\nوَّجَآءَ رَبُّكَ وَالْمَلَكُ صَفًّا صَفًّا ۚ‏(22)\nWA JAAA-A RABBOKA WAL-MALAKO SAFFAN SAFFAA.\nAnd cometh (the Command of) thy Lord, with the angels in ranges arrayed\nوَجِاىْٓءَ يَوْمَئِذٍۢ بِجَهَنَّمَ ۙ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَّتَذَكَّرُ الْاِنْسَانُ وَاَنّٰى لَهُ الذِّكْرٰىؕ‏(23)\nWA JEEE-A YAWMAEZIM BE-JAHANNAMA, YAWMA-EZIN-Y YATAZAKKARUL INSAANO WA ANNAA LAHUZ ZIKRAA.\nAnd the Hell shall be made to appear that Day, (and) that Day shall man get awakened, but of what avail unto him shall be the awakening?\nيَقُوْلُ يٰلَيْتَنِىْ قَدَّمْتُ لِحَيَاتِىۚ‏(24)\nYAQOOLO YAA LAYTANEE QADDAMTO LE-HAYAATEE.\nHe shall say: ‘‘Oh! Would that I had sent before (provisions for) my life!\nفَيَوْمَئِذٍ لَّا يُعَذِّبُ عَذَابَهٗۤ اَحَدٌ ۙ‏(25)\nFA-YAWMA-EZIL LAA YO-A’ZZEBO A’ZAABAHU AHADUNW.\nFor, on that day shall chastise not any one like unto His chastisement\nوَّلَا يُوْثِقُ وَثَاقَهٗۤ اَحَدٌ ؕ‏(26)\nWA LAA YOOSEQO WASAAQAHU AHAD.\nAnd shall bind not any one like unto His binding\nيٰۤاَيَّتُهَا النَّفْسُ الْمُطْمَئِنَّةُۖ‏(27)\nYAA AYYATOHAN NAFSUL MUTMA-INNATUR.\n(It will be said unto some) ‘‘O’ tranquilled soul at (complete) rest!\nارْجِعِىْۤ اِلٰى رَبِّكِ رَاضِيَةً مَّرْضِيَّةً ۚ‏(28)\nJE-E’E ELAA RABBEKE RAAZEYATAM MARZIYYAH.\nReturn thou unto thy Lord! well-pleased (with Him), (and) His being well-pleased with thee\nفَادْخُلِىْ فِىْ عِبٰدِىۙ‏(29)\nFADKHOLEE FEE E’BAADEE.\nThus, enter thou amidst My Servants\nوَادْخُلِىْ جَنَّتِى‏(30)\nWAD KHOLEE JANNATEE.\nAnd enter thou into My Garden!",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 30 ayaat. Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) urged believers to recite this Surah in their prayers as it is the Surah of Imam Husayn (a.s.) and the one who recites it often will be in the company of Imam Husayn (a.s.) on the Day of Judgement.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the one who recites this Surah, Allah (s.w.t.) will forgive his sins amounting to ten times the number of people who recite this Surah. On the Day of Reckoning he will have a shining light. If this Surah is written as a talisman and then tied to one’s back, after which he goes into his wife, then Allah (s.w.t.) will give him a child who will be a means of pride and blessings for him."
}
